        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): chat workspace panel leaves an empty gap when collapsed",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the session workspace panel in the Control UI chat view wasted horizontal space on both sides of its toggle:\n\n- **Collapsed**, it still reserved a 52px empty rail on the right edge — a permanent dead gap with two orphaned icons floating in it. The panel looked half-closed instead of closed.\n- **Expanded**, it floated inside the content gutter with a rounded corner and a ~20px strip of dead background between the panel and the window edge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe panel now behaves like the docked terminal at the bottom of the shell:\n\n- **Collapsed**: the workbench grid drops the rail column entirely (`minmax(0, 1fr)` single column) and the expand toggle floats over the chat's top-right corner as a small glass button, matching the existing circular nav-toggle pattern. The decorative file icon in the collapsed strip was removed along with its now-dead CSS.\n- **Expanded**: the chat content area drops its right gutter and squares the card's right corners (guarded to viewports >1120px, where the rail actually renders), so the panel closes flush against the window edge.\n\nThe toggle keeps its accessible name (`Expand session workspace`) and `aria-expanded` state.\n\n## User Impact\n\nClosing the workspace panel gives the full width back to the chat; opening it docks the panel flush to the window edge like the terminal drawer. The expand control stays visible and clickable in the top-right corner, so the panel remains one click away.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Before** — collapsed panel still reserves an empty rail (note the gap on the right edge):\n\n![before: collapsed rail reserves an empty 52px column](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/before-collapsed.png)\n\n**After (collapsed)** — the rail takes no width; the expand toggle floats in the corner:\n\n![after: collapsed rail takes no width, floating expand toggle](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/after-collapsed.png)\n\n**After (expanded)** — the open panel docks flush to the window edge (no gutter, square corners), like the bottom terminal:\n\n![after: expanded workspace rail docked flush to the window edge](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/workspace-rail-collapse/after-expanded.png)\n\nValidation (at the rebased head, post Control UI refactor #100024):\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts` — 92 passed, including the collapsed-rail test asserting the workbench drops the rail column and the floating toggle stays reachable.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/e2e/chat-flow.e2e.test.ts` — 19 passed (Playwright), covering collapse → expand → collapse round-trips, the new flush-edge assertion (`window.innerWidth - rail.getBoundingClientRect().right === 0` when expanded), and the ≤1120px viewport where the rail hides entirely.\n- Screenshots captured with the repo's Playwright e2e harness (mock gateway, light theme, 1360×860@2x).\n- `oxfmt --check` and `scripts/run-oxlint.mjs` clean on touched files.\n",
        "branch": "claude/angry-bardeen-3f4ca1",
